  "product": "GTS",
  "name": "Yoi Sweep Slow",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "The oo-ee-yoi sweep: a slow vowel that glides across half a bar and back, like a voice talking at F1. A Vowel-table layer and a Reed layer run through a Formant filter, and a triangle locked to 1/2 (a whole sweep per bar at 140 to 150 BPM) walks the filter through the vowels while the Vowel table opens a little with it. A clean sine sub sits at the played pitch and a low-pass tames the top, so the low end stays steady and mono. Play: held F1 to A#1 notes with the transport running, or a half-note riff. Macros: Vowel Sweep widens how far the mouth travels, Vowel Position slides where the sweep rests along the vowel row from A toward U, Sharpness narrows the vowel peaks so they ring, Grit pushes the tube drive for a louder, rougher voice.",
